{
  "dom_id": "step-q163054",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x{y}^{2}$ is enclosed between the curve $x={y}^{2}$ and $y$-axis for $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis.",
  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14121640/assets/34c6fb2eead75cb5217e7b33b5b98400b3f82e8ec29c91de9b8db5b22cefa6d7.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x{y}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{y}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{{y}^{7}}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{8}}{16}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
